UID:42095-1779804000-1779807600@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:DEMO: Container Gardening: Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spaces\, Wychwood Library
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing season\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies? This demonstration will start with how to choose soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize their positive impact on the environment. At the end of the demonstration\, materials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last.\n– Can be classified as part of Our Fragile Planet program series
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/demo-container-gardening-supporting-our-local-pollinators-in-small-spaces-wychwood-library/
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library – Wychwood\, 1431 Bathurst Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 3J2\, Canada
END:VEVENT
